{#
	The results block - everything that goes INSIDE div.results.

	Rendered by Zyppy\Search\Search\ResultRenderer, which is the SINGLE renderer
	for both paths: ZyppySearchController server-renders it into the fragment for
	the first page, and SearchController returns the identical string as the
	`html` field of the JSON the live search fetches. So first paint and every
	live update are the same markup by construction, not by agreement.

	IDENTIFIER: flat `search_zyppy_results`, and this file must stay OUT of
	contao/templates/twig/. That directory carries a `.twig-root` marker, which
	would give everything beneath it a prefixed `category/name` identifier - and
	a prefixed identifier breaks Controller::getTemplateGroup(), which builds the
	searchTpl and customTpl dropdowns and throws for any identifier containing a
	slash. See tests/Template/TemplateIdentifierTest.php.

	Not selectable from the backend on purpose: `searchTpl` selects the per-RESULT
	template (search_zyppy), which is the one an editor has a reason to swap.
	Override this wrapper the ordinary Contao way, by shipping a project template
	of the same name.

	THE PAGER IS REAL LINKS, not buttons. `?keywords=...&page=2` is a
	query-string-only href, so it resolves against the current document whichever
	path rendered it - and it means pagination works with JavaScript disabled.
	search.js intercepts clicks on `a[data-zyppy-page]` and fetches instead of
	navigating; without JavaScript the browser just follows them.

	--------------------------------------------------------------------------
	ESCAPED vs |raw. Twig autoescapes; both |raw values below are deliberate.

	|raw:
	  header   MSC.sResults is `Results %s - %s of %s for <strong>%s</strong>`
	           and MSC.sEmpty is `No matches for <strong>%s</strong>` - both
	           CARRY MARKUP in the translation, so the string cannot be escaped
	           as a whole. The keyword interpolated into it is escaped in PHP at
	           sprintf() time instead; see ZyppySearchRunner::buildHeader().
	  results  the already-rendered, already-escaped result rows.

	Escaped, because they are data: hint, previousHref, nextHref, the labels and
	every number. The hrefs are generated by ResultRenderer::pageHref() rather
	than taken from user input, but they still escape - there is no reason for a
	generated URL to be the one place a quote gets through.
	--------------------------------------------------------------------------
#}
{% if header|default('') %}
	<p class="header">{{ header|raw }}</p>
{% endif %}
{% if hint|default('') %}
	<p class="info">{{ hint }}</p>
{% endif %}
{{ results|default('')|raw }}
{% if totalPages|default(0) > 1 %}
	<nav class="pagination">
		<ul>
			{% if previousHref|default('') %}
				<li class="previous"><a href="{{ previousHref }}" rel="prev" data-zyppy-page="{{ previousPage }}">{{ previousLabel|default('') }}</a></li>
			{% endif %}
			<li class="current"><span>{{ page|default(1) }} / {{ totalPages }}</span></li>
			{% if nextHref|default('') %}
				<li class="next"><a href="{{ nextHref }}" rel="next" data-zyppy-page="{{ nextPage }}">{{ nextLabel|default('') }}</a></li>
			{% endif %}
		</ul>
	</nav>
{% endif %}
